        "body": "<!-- details-user-run-20261009f --><p><strong>Verified detail sources (October 9, 2026, SOA case review):</strong> Open Society Foundations\u2019 direct fellowship biography uses he/him for Baltimore community organizer Gary Ashbeck. SOA Watch\u2019s January 2004 press release identifies Jonah House\u2019s Baltimore resident among those arrested November 23, 2003; Joe Mulligan\u2019s participant account confirms he remained jailed after refusing bond. This matches the existing SOA case. No prison start or release date is calculated from time served. <a href=\"https://www.opensocietyfoundations.org/newsroom/2010-audacious-entrepreneurs-new-class-baltimore-community-fellows\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Source 1</a>. <a href=\"https://www.scoop.co.nz/stories/WO0401/S00122/americans-on-trial-for-protesting-terror-training.htm\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Source 2</a>. <a href=\"https://jonahhouse.org/archive/Mulligan%2CJoe_prison%20reflection.htm\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Source 3</a>.</p>",
        "under_review": 0,
